     "objectives": [
      {
       "id": "d_intro1",
       "task": "dialog",
       "description": "<i>Test run.</i> No shards are needed.<br><br>The four shards fit together in your hands, and the seams vanish. They were never broken. They were an invitation.<br><br>They pull you down, past where Crownhold's stair ends, into a hall of glass. Every pane holds a face. The Deck Warden. The Captain. The guards you cut down. Their eyes are open, and none of them blink.",
       "sceneBackground": "5emzv4rAEFL2iE6Vg5Znm",
       "sceneCharacters": [],
       "nextObjectiveId": [
        {
         "text": "Go deeper",
         "nextObjectiveId": "d_intro2"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "id": "d_intro2",
       "task": "dialog",
       "description": "She hangs in the air before the Mother Glass, her fan open behind her like a halo.<br><br>\"Lovely, aren't they? Every one of them held still for me.\" She smiles at the faces. \"The ship, the castle, all of it. I never lost them. I kept them.\"<br><br>\"And you have been cutting them out of my glass, one by one. How interesting.\"",
       "sceneBackground": "5emzv4rAEFL2iE6Vg5Znm",
       "sceneCharacters": [],
       "nextObjectiveId": [
        {
         "text": "You did this",
         "nextObjectiveId": "d_open"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "id": "d_open",
       "task": "dialog",
       "description": "She studies you the way she studied them. \"There is room in the glass for one more.\"<br><br>She turns to the wall, as if choosing a place for you. Her shadow does not turn with her. It stays where it was. Then it stands up off the floor.",
